[Music]  okay i was expecting to roast all these  drinks and be like a  like a snob but like i haven't had a bad  drink yet  [Music]  hi what's up my name is chris and i  worked as a barista  at voltaire in san jose and people  always ask baristas have you ever served  a celebrity  i haven't but i see a lot of people  leaking celebrity orders online  and i thought i'd try to make some of  them at home and see if they're any good  i know ariana grande had that one coffee  line in that one song that was  everywhere last year  apparently now she's like a starbucks  ambassador and she has her own secret  menu drink called the ariana grande  frappuccino  doesn't make that much sense because  she's vegan but it does sound really  good  it's gonna start off with a vanilla bean  frappuccino which apparently doesn't  have coffee in it so i'm gonna use  vanilla bean ice cream with milk and  ice and i'm gonna add in raspberry syrup  i couldn't find that syrup anywhere so i  just use raspberry preserves  and turn it into a syrup on the stove by  adding water and a little bit more sugar  i'm surprised the raspberry jam into  syrup thing turned out as well as it did  then we got chocolate chips chocolate  syrup and i'm gonna mix that in and  blend it all  then obviously gotta serve it in a clear  glass top it with whipped cream and a  little bit of caramel  okay yeah yeah that's that's really good  but i don't know what else i was  expecting  because it's literally just an icy  milkshake which is always going to be  good  so it definitely would have been better  if i used full fat ice cream  and milk that's probably where the  raspberry comes into play because it's a  little bit acidic and acid  generally tends to cut through fats  that's why people use like lemon juice  vinegar lime whenever they make like  really fatty meats  this is coming out of nowhere but i feel  like a pinch of salt you know like  salted caramel  i don't know why that would make it  better now charlie d emilio recently did  a partnership with  duncan on a drink called the charlie i'm  gonna taste test this recipe using the  actual  dunkin cold brew packets and i'm just  gonna follow the instructions that they  give on the box  i'm gonna measure out all of my water  just to make sure i'm not messing this  up  i think four cups is like 950  milliliters or something like that  and i'm gonna saran wrap the top of my  container and put it in the fridge  overnight  it's been about 12 hours and i took the  cold brew out and  made the charlie right over here it's  just cold brew with milk  and caramel i have no clue what a  caramel pump is  so i just went with three tablespoons  it's supposed to be three pumps  so i'm gonna taste test the pure cold  brew on its own just because i don't  wanna do dunkin dirty like that i don't  to mess up the recipe  and then like not like it  okay i kind of messed up because i got  donuts last night so my mouth is already  really clammy and sticky  so the caramel definitely doesn't help  that much okay so a few things to note  one as expected it is a super dark  really low acidity kind of bitter roast  and that makes a lot of sense because  they probably expect people to drink it  with milk  and this kind of a coffee bean holds  itself up to milk really well  and it has a really light body in the  sense that the mouth feel in your mouth  feels physically like water but it is  super strong i know the whole flavor  notes thing is super pretentious but  i'm not getting anything specific in  here maybe  chocolaty nutty kind of stuff no  fruitiness  or tartness or bright sweetness in the  coffee itself  and that makes a lot of sense because  they're probably trying to appeal to as  many people as possible by using a  really balanced blend  and it tastes exactly like you would  expect traditional  coffee to taste like i used to think  that i would never  ever drink coffee black but that's just  because i was using really dark roasts  from large commercial brands  they really try to sell you on that  saying that it's stronger but you can  get a stronger flavor  in lighter or medium roast just by the  way that you brew it  and dark roast tend to hide  inconsistencies and imperfections in  beans but yeah i really like this  back to ariana grande she partnered with  starbucks on another drink  called the cloud macchiato it looks cool  because it has this really fluffy foam  that they call  cloudfoam and i think we can replicate  that by using  icing sugar and powdered egg whites  which i got in the form of meringue  powder  i got some of the starbucks espresso  beans but i don't have an espresso  machine so  i try to make something that's just  close enough  by dialing it in on a mocha pot and no  it's technically  not espresso like it doesn't have enough  pressure so you don't end up with that  crema on top  but like come on i tasted it before  putting in the milk and it's close  enough  like relax i'll take it off the stove  once it starts bubbling and i'll run it  under cold water to stop the extraction  it should give me about 45 to 50 grams  or so  and then i got to make the foam i don't  have an electric mixer so we're gonna  have to whip this one by hand  which gives me really bad flashbacks to  dow gonna coffee  so i brought an elbow brace just in case  of tendonitis  yeah whipping anything by hand takes  about like 20 years or so  um it's about the journey not the  destination or something like that  put some milk and then get a spoon and  make it look all nice  look at that and then they make this  waffle thing with the caramel  here we have it right here all of the  normal sized cups were in the dishwasher  but this is actually closer to the  traditional  macchiato size the italian macchiato is  just two shots of espresso  with a tiny little dollop of foamy milk  on top this is not the starbucks  macchiato because they do it like  backwards theirs is like a  latte macchiato but the typical cafe  macchiato or espresso macchiato is like  barely any milk and it's like  that small so let's go ahead and try it  okay i was expecting to roast all these  drinks and be like a  like a snob but like i haven't had a bad  drink yet um but the caramel on top is  actually is it caramel or caramel  the caramel caramel the caramel's a nice  touch i feel like all starbucks drinks  are kind of the same thing it's just  like  vaguely milky coffee kind of flavor with  some hit  of sweetness yeah the foam barely tastes  like anything  so i try to find other interesting  coffee orders everyone else just gets  soy lattes but in an interview  khloe kardashian said that she gets a  venti  seven pump no water chai latte first of  all chai  is just tea so it has to have water  second how is it a pump what i think  they mean is that they just brew chai  tea and then  reduce it down to like a concentrate  that they use as a syrup and then when  they serve it they just cut it with  water to make it back into tea and then  make the latte so chloe probably just  wants to concentrate with the milk  i saw that starbucks on their website  shows what's in their chai  and i could do that from scratch but  it's kind of similar to this tea bag  that i found at the grocery store  i'm going to use seven bags and then  reduce it down into a syrup with sugar  that's  roughly what seven pumps would be in  volume and then make the latte out of  that let's go ahead and try it  okay that's not bad if i had to pick a  least favorite one it would probably be  this one but  i'm surprised that it's pretty spicy and  it cuts through the milk pretty well  i learned a few things one you can make  a dessert taste fancier just by adding  some kind of  acidic tart fruit even if the dessert  itself  isn't supposed to be acidic or tart i  learned that cold brew packets work  you can just make syrups on the stove  and foam  is exhausting  [Music]

